@import "Exercise_8_19.lean"

**EXERCISE 8.19.** Suppose we know both

$$T \quad \text{and} \quad E \to E \trianglelefteq E \ .$$

Does it follow that $E + E$ and $E \times E \trianglelefteq E$?

The development is with the [Sum and product retracts](1980_SumProdRetracts.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`example_819`).** Domains closed under arrow also admit sum and product retracts.

*Proof.* By assembling the peer lemmas named in the packaging module. ∎
